#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# angle_vector

#% text
# `angle_vector(phi)` gives the unit vector `[cos(phi), sin(phi)]`; `angle_vector([r, phi])` gives the point with polar coordinates `r`, `phi`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `angle_vector([r, theta, phi])` gives the point of spherical coordinates, `theta` measured from the z axis and `phi` in the xy plane.

#% item
# `angle_vector(c, p)` gives the same point relative to the point `c` (the sum `c + angle_vector(p)`).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
angle_vector(a)
#% output
#= [cos(a), sin(a)]

#% cell
angle_vector([2, pi/3])
#% output
#= [1, 3^(1/2)]

#% cell
angle_vector([1, a, b])
#% output
#= [cos(b)*sin(a), sin(a)*sin(b), cos(a)]

#% cell
angle_vector([1, 1], pi/2)
#% output
#= [1, 2]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `from_polar_coordinates`, `vector_angle`
